# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEBASER.SITE environment - production builds
#
# This file is committed on purpose, and it holds nothing secret: every value is
# a NEXT_PUBLIC_* one, which reaches the browser in the bundle anyway. The
# publishable (anon) key is meant to be public - Row Level Security in
# supabase/schema.sql is what protects the data, on every table and in the
# avatars bucket.
#
# It exists so a deploy runs on Supabase without a dashboard step: Next.js loads
# .env.production for `next build`, which is what Vercel runs. If the same names
# are set in the Vercel project they win over this file, so this can also be
# deleted once they are set there - see supabase/README.md, step 4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://uekreahyooezywjgzirr.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_mAvbOhIWz75GxaJG_IRGIw_LfDCZ348

# Where each part of the site keeps its data. All four point at the tables
# created by supabase/schema.sql; drop one back to the mock store by deleting its
# line here and in .env.local.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BACKEND=supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORUM_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROFILE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMS_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_MUSIC_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_LORE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
